        "original_id": "5633f999-4bfe-5783-8fb4-6782e58af010",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mike Connors, Leon Danielian, Alec Guinness, Robert Redford\n- Works: Mannix, Situation Hopeless... But Not Serious, Sacred Planet\n- Roles: actor, ballet dancer, teacher, choreographer, educator, narrator\n- Awards: Golden Globe Award, Emmy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Leon Danielian was born on 31 October 1920 and was an American ballet dancer, teacher, choreographer, and educator.\n- Mike Connors was born Krekor Ohanian on August 15, 1925 and was an Armenian-American actor.\n- Situation Hopeless... But Not Serious is a 1965 comedy film starring Alec Guinness, Mike Connors, and Robert Redford.\n- Mike Connors played private detective Joe Mannix in the CBS television series Mannix from 1967 to 1975.\n- Mike Connors won a Golden Globe Award in 1970 for Mannix, the first of six straight nominations, and he also received four consecutive Emmy nominations from 1970 through 1973.\n- Leon Danielian died on 8 March 1997.\n- Robert Redford provided narration for the film Sacred Planet.\n- Mike Connors died on January 26, 2017.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
